From da6c917aaf5553e52a1b0de2584a1e1227fae3af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Ottenhoff <alexander.ottenhoff@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:03:05 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Android: native window, RGBA8 presentation and smaller
 texture cache

- Application window: SDL display bounds, fullscreen window and ANativeWindow handle.
- Present RGBA8 on Android (the only format Android surfaces guarantee) and
  build the VI pipeline for the same format.
- 1024-entry texture descriptor arrays on Android.
- Integer-scale resolution rounds down on Android.
- Pick DXC by host CPU and allow a host file_to_c (RT64_HOST_FILE_TO_C) for cross builds.

Adapted from linkzenic's rt64 Android port (Zelda64Recomp-Android) and
DKR-R's rt64-rgba-presentation patch.
